<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Waters Corp to create 115 new jobs in Wexford.</title>
<headline>Waters Corp to create 115 new jobs in Wexford.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Irish government said on Tuesday that Waters Corporation had agreed to a 3.7 million punt investment proposal to set up a new European base in Wexford which would create 115 jobs.</p>
<p>Waters is a U.S.-based manufacturer of performance liquid chromatography analytical instruments.</p>
<p>A government statement said that IDA Ireland, the state-owned industrial development agency, is also at an advanced stage of negotiations with a U.S. engineering company to establish a facility in Kilkenny which would create up to 150 jobs.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
